      "title": "Exercice final : partie 1",
      "body": "Cet exercice mélange les compétences de la partie 1 : forme algébrique, conjugué et module, plan complexe, équations du second degré. Chaque réussite rapporte un bonus d’XP.",
      "example": {
        "statement": "Écrire $\\dfrac{1}{1 - i}$ sous forme algébrique.",
        "solution": "$\\dfrac{1}{1 - i} = \\dfrac{1 + i}{(1 - i)(1 + i)} = \\dfrac{1 + i}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{2} + \\dfrac{1}{2}\\,i$."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "EXERCISE",
      "exercise": {
        "code": "B1-E1",
        "type": "NUMERIC",
        "skill": "Quotient",
        "payload": {
          "prompt": "Écrire $\\dfrac{3 + i}{1 - 2i}$ sous forme algébrique.",
          "format": "complex",
          "placeholder": "ex. 1/5 + 7/5 i"
        },
        "answer": {
          "re": 0.2,
          "im": 1.4,
          "tolerance": 0.001
        },
        "solution": "$\\dfrac{3 + i}{1 - 2i} = \\dfrac{(3 + i)(1 + 2i)}{5} = \\dfrac{3 + 6i + i - 2}{5} = \\dfrac{1 + 7i}{5}$.",
        "hint": "Multipliez par le conjugué du dénominateur."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "EXERCISE",
      "exercise": {
        "code": "B1-E2",
        "type": "NUMERIC",
        "skill": "Module",
        "payload": {
          "prompt": "Calculer le module de $\\dfrac{3 + i}{1 - 2i}$. Valeur exacte ou approchée à $10^{-2}$ près.",
          "format": "real",
          "placeholder": "ex. sqrt(2)"
        },
        "answer": {
          "value": 1.4142135623730951,
          "tolerance": 0.01
        },
        "solution": "$\\left|\\dfrac{3 + i}{1 - 2i}\\right| = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\sqrt{2}$.",
        "hint": "Le module d’un quotient est le quotient des modules."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "EXERCISE",
      "exercise": {
        "code": "B1-E3",
        "type": "NUMERIC",
        "skill": "Second degré",
        "payload": {
          "prompt": "Résoudre $z^2 - 2z + 5 = 0$ : donner la solution dont la partie imaginaire est positive.",
          "format": "complex",
          "placeholder": "ex. 1 + 2i"
        },
        "answer": {
          "re": 1,
          "im": 2,
          "tolerance": 0.001
        },
        "solution": "$\\Delta = 4 - 20 = -16$ donc $z = \\dfrac{2 \\pm 4i}{2} = 1 \\pm 2i$.",
        "hint": "$\\Delta < 0$ : solutions $\\dfrac{-b \\pm i\\sqrt{-\\Delta}}{2a}$."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "EXERCISE",
      "exercise": {
        "code": "B1-E4",
        "type": "QCM",
        "skill": "Conjugué",
        "payload": {
          "prompt": "Pour $z = 2 - 3i$, quelles affirmations sont vraies ? (plusieurs réponses possibles)",
